  "description": {
    "text": "The Kamex Mega Battle of 2016 was Japan's spring championship, named after the 1998 series: tournaments in Nagoya on 5 May, at Intex Osaka on 15 May, Makuhari Messe on 21 and 22 May and Fukuoka on 29 May 2016, and a Japan Championship at Tokyo Big Sight's TFT Hall on 19 June whose top finishers were invited to the World Championships in San Francisco that August. Two straight wins in the Second Stage earned a Fighting Fury Belt, and Play Points from it and the side events bought prizes such as Crobat BREAK for three points or the pair M Garchomp-EX and Garchomp Spirit Link for six. Visitors who took a photo at the PokéKyun♥ Photo Spot got a holo Pikachu. Its Victory Battle, on the first day in Chiba, has its own entry.",
    "sources": [
      {
